From d06312a0473b856aef138611eeb703c4408dce84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 15:22:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(integrity): assumption provenance, output versioning,
 honest deliverable claims
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The PDF is the artefact a customer forwards to an owner, a bank or a
Stadtwerk. It was presenting twelve unsourced default inputs, a CO2 factor, a
hard-coded 2 %/a opex escalation that appeared in no UI at all, and a "6-10 %
IRR" band the brief itself calls a placeholder — all with the visual authority
of a finished report, signed with a personal Gmail, and with no version stamp,
so two reports produced months apart under different defaults were
indistinguishable.

- shared/assumptions.ts (new): SourceOfTruth register
  (OFFICIAL_SOURCE | CUSTOMER_PROVIDED | ENGINEERING_ESTIMATE | MARKET_DATA |
  HISTORICAL_DATA | PLACEHOLDER) for every input, plus the constants the engine
  applies WITHOUT exposing them (2 %/a opex escalation, 0.38 t/MWh CO2 factor,
  the benchmark band). Invariant, enforced by test: verified === true requires
  a reference AND an asOf date. Everything ships verified:false, which is the
  honest state today.
- Provenance is resolved per VALUE, not per field: the moment a customer edits
  an input it stops being our placeholder and becomes their statement about
  their project. The report says which is which.
- Versioning (P0.6): model_version, assumption_set, calculation_date,
  jurisdiction=DE, currency=EUR, scenario — stamped in the page chrome of every
  page and repeated as a reproducibility line. buildReportDoc takes an
  injectable clock so output is deterministic under test.
- New PDF section "Herkunft der Annahmen" + a warning block naming every value
  in THIS report that is not verified.
- interpret.ts: the benchmark line no longer claims "typische
  Mieterstrom-Projekte erreichen 6-10 %". It states an internal orientation
  range with no sourced basis, and shares constants with the register so prose
  and provenance table cannot drift.
- P0.5: personal Gmail removed from the report contact block.
- Removes a promise the product does not keep: the lead-capture band advertised
  a "Messkonzept-Skizze nach §42b EnWG" that the PDF has never contained.
  Regression test asserts the report makes no such claim.
- Drops the hard-coded legal cite from the marketing-consent copy.
- Fixes a silent rendering defect: jsPDF's built-in Helvetica is WinAnsi, so
  U+2082 had no glyph and "CO₂-Einsparung" printed as "CO ,-Einsparung".

The math is untouched: all 12 engine tests unchanged and green.

Evidence: pnpm check clean (both projects), 57/57 vitest (7 new + 6 upgraded
PDF assertions that search the RENDERED document, not just the functions),
pnpm build clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
